Apple device-management schemas
  https://github.com/apple/device-management
  Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Apple Inc.
  MIT License (see LICENSE.txt in that repository)

  scripts/fetch_schema.py downloads the YAML files under mdm/profiles/ at
  runtime and caches them in ~/.cache/mobileconfig-builder/. None of these
  files are vendored into this repository, and none are redistributed with
  it. The cache holds a verbatim copy of Apple's files; the MIT license
  above applies to that copy.

ProfileManifests
  https://github.com/ProfileManifests/ProfileManifests
  No license.

  This repository carries no LICENSE file, and the GitHub API reports
  "license": null (checked 2026-09-04). Without a license there is no grant
  to redistribute, so nothing from it is vendored here and nothing ships in
  the release archive. scripts/fetch_schema.py fetches a single manifest at
  runtime, only when you pass --manifests, and caches it under
  ~/.cache/mobileconfig-builder/profilemanifests/<ref>/. That copy is yours,
  made by you, on your machine. Whether you may pass it on is a question for
  the upstream project, not one this repository can answer.

  The manifests are maintained by the Mac Admins community and also power
  ProfileCreator and iMazing Profile Editor. They are not an Apple source.
  Where Apple describes a payload type, this tool ignores the manifest.
